@cc [owner:pmilliotte,label:architecture] resource-methods-take-caller-transaction
Resource methods that read or write FDB MUST take the caller's `&Transaction` and MUST NOT call
`fdb::with_transaction` or open a transaction themselves, so a caller can combine several resource
calls in one atomic transaction.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:architecture;error-handling] cross-resource-error-propagation
Fallible resource methods MUST use their own concrete `Error` type, directly or through
`storage::Error<Error>`, rather than a caller-selected error type. Propagated domain errors from
another resource MUST appear as explicit typed variants, such as
`session::Error::Tenant(tenant::Error)`. Cross-resource `From` conversions MUST support `?`, wrapping
only `storage::Error::Resource` and preserving all other variants, including FDB failures, unchanged.
API translation MUST delegate wrapped domain errors to the originating resource's status mapping.
